    <bpmn:process id="W_W1204" name="W1204. Store-Level Business Continuity Plan (BCP) Annual Update, Tabletop Exercise &amp; Certification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual BCP review cycle (Q1 each year); or triggered by major incident at any store, new store opening, or significant operational change
Frequency: Annual per store; 200 stores reviewed on rolling schedule (~40/month over 5 months in Q1–Q2)
Volume: 200 store-level BCPs + 4 DC-level BCPs + 1 HQ BCP = 205 total
Owner: Business Continuity Manager
Participants: BC Manager, Store Manager, VP Store Operations, IT Disaster Recovery Lead, Insurance Coordinator, Regional Manager
Source: workflow W1204 — Store-Level Business Continuity Plan (BCP) Annual Update, Tabletop Exercise &amp; Certification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1204_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1204_Lane1" name="BC Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1204_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1204_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1204_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1204_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1204_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1204_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1204_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1204_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1204_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1204_Start4" name="Annual BCP review cycle (Q1 each year); or triggered by major incident at any store, new…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1204_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1204_Task5" name="BCP template update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: BCP template update: BC Manager reviews and updates the standardized store-level BCP template: (a) updates contact lists (regional management, emergency services, insurance hotline, ACS contact, bank branch), (b) updates escalation procedures, (c) updates recovery time objectives (RTO): POS operations ≤ 4 hours, full store operations ≤ 24 hours, normal operations ≤ 72 hours, (d) incorporates lessons learned from incidents in the past year, (e) distributes updated template to all Store Managers
Responsible (R): BC Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 8 hours (template update)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1204_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1204_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1204_Task6" name="Store Manager BCP review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Store Manager BCP review: Each Store Manager reviews and customizes the BCP template for their specific location: (a) identifies location-specific risks (flood-prone area, earthquake zone, high-crime area), (b) lists local emergency contacts (barangay captain, nearest fire station, nearest hospital, police station), (c) documents alternative operating procedures (reduced POS terminals, manual operations per W580, limited product categories), (d) identifies pre-approved local contractors for emergency repairs, (e) documents cash float emergency procedure if armored car cannot access store
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2 hours/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1204_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1204_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1204_Task7" name="Tabletop exercise execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Tabletop exercise execution: BC Manager facilitates annual tabletop exercise for each store (can be conducted in batches of 10–15 stores via video conference): (a) presents a scenario (typhoon Signal No. 4, fire in backroom, 48-hour system outage, flooding), (b) Store Manager walks through their BCP response step-by-step, (c) BC Manager evaluates response quality: communication timeliness, escalation appropriateness, resource awareness, customer/safety prioritization, (d) identifies gaps and assigns corrective actions
Responsible (R): BC Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1 hour/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1204_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1204_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1204_Task8" name="Gap remediation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Gap remediation: For gaps identified in Step 3: (a) Store Manager updates BCP to address gaps within 2 weeks, (b) BC Manager reviews updated BCP and confirms closure, (c) critical gaps (e.g., no emergency power plan, no communication backup) require immediate remediation within 48 hours
Responsible (R): Store Manager / BC Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 1 hour/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1204_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1204_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1204_Task9" name="BCP certification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: BCP certification: BC Manager issues annual BCP certification for each location that: (a) BCP is current and location-specific, (b) Store Manager has completed tabletop exercise, (c) all gaps from tabletop exercise are remediated, (d) emergency contact lists are verified; certification status tracked in BCP dashboard; uncertified stores flagged for VP Store Operations attention
Responsible (R): BC Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 15 min/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1204_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1204_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1204_Task10" name="New store BCP onboarding">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: New store BCP onboarding: For each new store opening (10–15/year): BC Manager conducts dedicated BCP onboarding session with the new Store Manager during the pre-opening period (per W16/W702); tabletop exercise conducted within 30 days of opening; initial BCP certification issued upon successful tabletop completion
Responsible (R): BC Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 3 hours/new store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1204_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1204_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1204_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1204_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1204_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-228 (ensure BCP readiness &amp; insurance recovery.) | - operational: BCP onboarding for new Store Managers (W16) and requiring BCP review as part of new SM orientation; operational: batch video conference sessions (10–15 stores at a time) and alternating detailed vs. abbreviated exercises for low-risk locations; operational: mandatory annual update in Step 2 and trigger-based updates (staff turnover, phone number changes)
Owner: Business Continuity Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1204_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1204_Annotation12" targetRef="W1204_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
