    <bpmn:process id="W_W1322" name="W1322. IT Disaster Recovery (DR) Failover Test Execution, Validation &amp; Recovery Time Assessment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly IT DR testing calendar; or ad-hoc triggered by major system incident, IT infrastructure change, or regulatory audit requirement
Frequency: Quarterly full DR failover test (4×/year); monthly component-level tests for critical modules (POS, inventory)
Volume: 4 full failover tests + 12 component tests per year
Owner: CIO
Participants: CIO, Infrastructure Team, Applications Team, IT Security, BC Manager, COO (observer for quarterly tests)
Source: workflow W1322 — IT Disaster Recovery (DR) Failover Test Execution, Validation &amp; Recovery Time Assessment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1322_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1322_Lane1" name="CIO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1322_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1322_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1322_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1322_Lane2" name="Infrastructure Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1322_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1322_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1322_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1322_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1322_Lane3" name="Applications Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1322_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1322_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1322_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1322_Start5" name="Quarterly IT DR testing calendar; or ad-hoc triggered by major system incident, IT…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1322_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1322_Task6" name="Pre-test planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pre-test planning: CIO prepares DR test plan: (a) selects test scope: full failover (all systems) or component failover (POS only, inventory only, ecommerce only, financials only); (b) defines test window: typically Saturday midnight to Sunday 6 AM to minimize business impact; (c) identifies RTO targets to validate: POS ≤ 4 hours, inventory ≤ 6 hours, ecommerce ≤ 4 hours, financials ≤ 8 hours; (d) defines RPO targets: data loss ≤ 15 minutes (near-real-time replication); (e) notifies all stakeholders: Store Managers, DC Supervisors, ecommerce team, Finance — &quot;system maintenance window&quot; communication; (f) prepares rollback plan in case DR failover fails
Responsible (R): CIO
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4–6 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1322_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1322_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1322_Task7" name="Pre-failover data snapshot">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pre-failover data snapshot: Infrastructure Team captures baseline data: (a) record current transaction volumes (POS, ecommerce, AP/AR); (b) take database timestamp snapshot for data integrity comparison; (c) document current system performance metrics (response times, concurrent users, batch job status); (d) verify DR site replication is current: replication lag must be &lt; 5 minutes before proceeding
Responsible (R): Infrastructure Team
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1322_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1322_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1322_Task8" name="Failover execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Failover execution: Infrastructure Team executes failover: (a) primary site: gracefully stop all application services; (b) activate DR site: (i) promote DR database to primary, (ii) start application services on DR infrastructure, (iii) update DNS/load balancer to route traffic to DR site, (iv) verify network connectivity from stores and DCs to DR site; (c) start timer: record exact failover start time for RTO measurement; (d) monitor system health: CPU, memory, disk I/O, database connections, replication status
Responsible (R): Infrastructure Team
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1322_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1322_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1322_Task9" name="Functional validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Functional validation: Applications Team validates all critical functions at DR site: (a) POS: process test transactions at 2–3 volunteer stores (cash sale, card payment, return, price lookup, inventory check); verify near-real-time inventory sync; (b) Ecommerce: place test BOPIS order and test delivery order; verify inventory reservation and order confirmation; (c) Inventory: verify real-time stock levels match pre-failover snapshot; process test goods receipt and transfer order; (d) Procurement: verify PO creation and approval workflow; check vendor portal accessibility; (e) Finance: verify GL posting, AP invoice processing, AR statement generation; (f) HR/Payroll: verify employee self-service portal and time attendance access; (g) DC/WMS: verify RF gun connectivity and pick/pack/ship processing; (h) record any functional failures or degraded performance
Responsible (R): Applications Team
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1322_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1322_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1322_Task10" name="Performance validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Performance validation: Infrastructure Team measures DR site performance against production baselines: (a) POS transaction processing time: target &lt; 3 seconds per transaction per model company profile; (b) report generation: target &lt; 30 seconds for standard reports; (c) concurrent user capacity: verify DR site supports ≥ 500 concurrent users (50% of peak per NFR-028); (d) batch job processing: verify scheduled batch jobs (nightly inventory sync, daily sales posting) execute within normal time windows; (e) database query performance: compare average query response time to production baseline
Responsible (R): Infrastructure Team
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1322_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1322_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1322_Task11" name="Data integrity verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Data integrity verification: Applications Team compares post-failover data to pre-failover snapshot: (a) record count comparison for critical tables (inventory, orders, customers, GL entries); (b) verify no data loss: all transactions recorded between last replication and failover are present at DR site; (c) verify referential integrity: no orphaned records or broken cross-references; (d) calculate actual RPO: time difference between last replicated transaction and failover time
Responsible (R): Applications Team
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1322_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1322_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1322_Task12" name="Failback execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Failback execution: After validation: (a) Infrastructure Team executes failback to primary site: (i) replicate DR site data back to primary, (ii) stop DR site services, (iii) promote primary back to active, (iv) update DNS/load balancer, (v) verify connectivity; (b) verify all systems operational at primary site; (c) resume normal operations; (d) verify replication from primary to DR site resumes normally
Responsible (R): Infrastructure Team
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1322_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1322_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1322_Task13" name="Post-test report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Post-test report: CIO prepares DR test report: (a) test scope and objectives; (b) timeline: planned vs. actual failover and failback times; (c) RTO achievement: actual vs. target for each system; (d) RPO achievement: actual data loss (if any) vs. target; (e) functional test results: pass/fail by system; (f) performance test results: DR vs. production baseline; (g) data integrity verification results; (h) issues encountered: any failures, errors, or unexpected behavior; (i) recommendations: improvements to DR architecture, procedures, or training; (j) report submitted to COO and BC Manager for integration into BCP per W847
Responsible (R): CIO
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1322_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1322_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1322_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1322_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1322_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-228 (ensure BCP readiness &amp; insurance recovery.) | - operational: Saturday midnight test window and rollback plan; operational: near-real-time synchronous replication for critical databases and pre-failover replication lag check (Step 2); operational: rotating test responsibilities across Infrastructure Team members
Owner: CIO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1322_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1322_Annotation15" targetRef="W1322_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1322_Flow17" sourceRef="W1322_Start5" targetRef="W1322_Task6" />
