    <bpmn:process id="W_W1449" name="W1449. Volcanic Eruption &amp; Ashfall Business Continuity Protocol for BuildRight Stores and DCs" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: PHIVOLCS Alert Level 3 or higher for any Philippine volcano within 100 km of BuildRight operations; or significant ashfall reported in any BuildRight location area
Frequency: Volcanic events affecting BuildRight operations: estimated 1–2 events per year (Philippines has 24 active volcanoes; Mayon, Taal, Kanlaon, and Bulusan are most frequently active)
Volume: Each event may affect 10–80 stores depending on ashfall spread (wind direction dependent); DCs in Davao (near Mt. Apo), Calamba (near Taal), and Clark (near Pinatubo) are at elevated risk
Owner: BC Manager / COO
Participants: BC Manager, COO, Store Managers (affected), DC Managers, Facilities Engineer, COO, CHRO, IT Security, LP Officers
Source: workflow W1449 — Volcanic Eruption &amp; Ashfall Business Continuity Protocol for BuildRight Stores and DCs</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1449_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1449_Lane1" name="BC Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1449_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1449_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1449_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1449_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1449_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1449_Lane3" name="Facilities Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1449_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1449_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1449_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1449_Start5" name="PHIVOLCS Alert Level 3 or higher for any Philippine volcano within 100 km of BuildRight…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1449_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1449_Task6" name="Volcano monitoring activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Volcano monitoring activation (PHIVOLCS Alert Level 2+): BC Manager activates volcano monitoring protocol for affected region: (a) monitor PHIVOLCS bulletins every 4 hours, (b) identify stores and DCs within 50 km radius of volcano (primary impact zone) and 100 km radius (ashfall zone), (c) pre-position protective supplies: tarpaulins for outdoor inventory, N95 masks for staff, roof inspection for stores with aging roof structures, (d) brief Store Managers on potential closure timeline
Responsible (R): BC Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1449_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1449_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1449_Task7" name="Ashfall preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Ashfall preparation (Alert Level 3 or ashfall advisory): Affected Store Managers execute ashfall preparedness checklist: (a) cover outdoor lumber yard and building materials with heavy-duty tarpaulins (secured against wind), (b) protect paint mixing station — move paint inventory indoors and cover tinting machines, (c) cover rooftop HVAC units and generator intakes with filter material, (d) stage N95 masks at all entrances for customer and staff use, (e) inspect roof drainage — clear gutters to prevent ash accumulation (wet ash is extremely heavy: 10 cm wet ash = ~100 kg/m², potentially collapsing roofs)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Maintenance
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4–6 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1449_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1449_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1449_Task8" name="Controlled closure">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Controlled closure (Alert Level 4 or heavy ashfall): (a) Store Manager executes controlled closure per W850: complete current transactions, secure cash, protect merchandise, send staff home with safety advisory, (b) DC Manager secures DC: cover dock doors, protect inventory above ash contamination level, secure hazardous materials, (c) Facilities Engineer assesses roof loading risk: if ash accumulation &gt; 5 cm and rain is forecast (wet ash risk), authorize emergency roof clearing by maintenance team if safe to do so
Responsible (R): Store Manager / DC Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1449_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1449_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1449_Task9" name="Post-eruption damage assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Post-eruption damage assessment (when PHIVOLCS downgrades to Alert Level 2 and local authorities permit access): (a) Facilities Engineer and LP Officer conduct site inspection: (i) roof structural assessment (ash loading, corrosion), (ii) HVAC system contamination check, (iii) outdoor inventory damage assessment (lumber, tiles, cement — ash contamination), (iv) electronic equipment check (POS terminals, computers — ash infiltration), (v) vehicle fleet inspection (ash in engines, filters), (b) document damage with photos for insurance claims per W853, (c) classify each store/DC: (i) safe to reopen (minor cleaning required), (ii) requires repair before reopening, (iii) severely damaged (extended closure)
Responsible (R): Facilities Engineer / LP Officer
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4–8 hours per site</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1449_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1449_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1449_Task10" name="Ash cleanup and reopening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Ash cleanup and reopening: For stores classified as safe to reopen: (a) professional ash cleanup: (i) wet ash removal from roof (prevent secondary contamination), (ii) clean and test HVAC systems before reactivation, (iii) wash outdoor merchandise (lumber, tiles) — many items are cleanable with water, (iv) replace air filters in POS terminals and computers, (v) clean parking lot and entrances (ash is slippery when wet), (b) COO authorizes reopening only after Facilities Engineer certifies structural safety, (c) Store Manager communicates reopening to customers via social media and WhatsApp groups per W1443
Responsible (R): Facilities Engineer / Store Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1–3 days per store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1449_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1449_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1449_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1449_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1449_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-319 (ensure controlled execution — BCP Planning &amp; Testing (PA-26.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: BC Manager / COO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
