    <bpmn:process id="W_W1450" name="W1450. Earthquake Response Protocol, Structural Assessment &amp; Store Reopening Safety Verification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: PHIVOLCS earthquake alert: Intensity V (Strong) or higher in any BuildRight location area; or store/DC structural damage reported by staff; or LGU-mandated building inspection order
Frequency: Significant earthquakes (Intensity V+) affecting BuildRight operations: estimated 2–4 events per year in the Philippines (seismically active region on the Pacific Ring of Fire)
Volume: Each event may affect 5–50+ stores depending on epicenter location and depth; Mindanao (active fault lines near Davao HQ and DC1) and Metro Manila (West Valley Fault) are highest risk areas
Owner: COO / Facilities Engineer
Participants: COO, Facilities Engineer, Store Manager, DC Manager, BC Manager, LP Officer, Local Structural Engineer (contracted), CHRO, IT Security
Source: workflow W1450 — Earthquake Response Protocol, Structural Assessment &amp; Store Reopening Safety Verification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1450_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1450_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1450_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1450_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1450_Lane2" name="Facilities Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1450_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1450_Lane3" name="Structural Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1450_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1450_Lane4" name="COO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1450_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1450_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1450_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1450_Start6" name="PHIVOLCS earthquake alert: Intensity V (Strong) or higher in any BuildRight location…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1450_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1450_Task7" name="Immediate earthquake response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Immediate earthquake response (during/within minutes of shaking): (a) Store Manager/DC Manager executes &quot;Duck, Cover, Hold&quot; protocol for all personnel and customers, (b) when shaking stops: initiate evacuation per building evacuation plan — all personnel and customers assemble at designated outdoor assembly point (parking lot, away from building, power lines, and outdoor lumber yard), (c) Store Manager accounts for all staff and any customers who were in the building — report missing persons to emergency services, (d) provide first aid for injuries (stores have first aid kits per W631), (e) secure building perimeter — no re-entry until structural assessment is complete
Responsible (R): Store Manager / DC Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1450_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1450_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1450_Task8" name="Rapid visual structural assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Rapid visual structural assessment (within 1–2 hours of earthquake): (a) Facilities Engineer or trained LP Officer conducts rapid external visual assessment of each affected store/DC: (i) visible structural damage: cracked walls, collapsed roof, leaning structure, ground settlement, (ii) utility hazards: gas leaks (smell), electrical hazards (downed power lines), water main breaks, (iii) fallen merchandise/shelving inside (visible through windows), (iv) outdoor area: lumber yard collapse, fence/wall collapse, (b) classify each building: (i) GREEN — no visible damage, likely safe for rapid reopening, (ii) YELLOW — minor visible damage, requires engineering inspection before reopening, (iii) RED — significant visible damage, unsafe, do not enter until professional structural engineering assessment complete, (c) report classification to COO for chain-wide status dashboard
Responsible (R): Facilities Engineer / LP Officer
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 30–60 min per site</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1450_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1450_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1450_Task9" name="Professional structural engineering inspection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Professional structural engineering inspection (within 24–72 hours for YELLOW/RED buildings): (a) COO engages contracted structural engineers (pre-qualified and on retainer for rapid deployment), (b) engineer conducts detailed inspection: (i) foundation and structural frame integrity, (ii) roof connection points, (iii) wall cracks (measure width — &gt; 5mm may indicate structural compromise), (iv) floor slab condition, (v) dock door alignment (DCs), (vi) fire suppression system integrity, (c) engineer issues written safety certification: (i) SAFE for immediate reopening, (ii) SAFE WITH RESTRICTIONS (e.g., &quot;no heavy merchandise on top shelves&quot;), (iii) UNSAFE — requires repair before occupancy, (d) Buildings rated UNSAFE: COO plans repair project per W96 (renovation), including insurance claim per W853
Responsible (R): Structural Engineer / COO
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4–8 hours per building</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1450_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1450_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1450_Task10" name="Phased store reopening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Phased store reopening: COO authorizes reopening based on safety certification: (a) GREEN buildings: reopen immediately (after internal cleanup — fallen merchandise, shelf resets), (b) YELLOW buildings cleared as SAFE: reopen after engineering-required fixes (e.g., re-anchoring shelves, patching walls), (c) RED buildings: remain closed until repaired and re-certified; Store Manager communicates closure to customers via social media and redirects to nearest open BuildRight store, (d) DC reopening: Logistics Manager reroutes deliveries to alternative DC if primary DC is RED; activate inter-DC transfer per W22 to replenish stores from unaffected DCs
Responsible (R): COO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1450_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1450_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1450_Task11" name="Post-earthquake operational recovery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-earthquake operational recovery (T+1 day to T+2 weeks): (a) inventory damage assessment: identify merchandise damaged by falling, crushing, or contamination, (b) IT systems check: verify POS, network, and payment systems operational at reopened stores, (c) supply chain recovery: assess vendor and logistics partner impact; activate alternative sourcing per W763 if primary vendors are earthquake-affected, (d) HR: check on employee safety and welfare; activate employee assistance program for affected staff, (e) insurance: initiate claims for structural damage and inventory loss per W853
Responsible (R): COO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1450_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1450_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1450_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1450_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1450_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-319 (ensure controlled execution — BCP Planning &amp; Testing (PA-26.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: COO / Facilities Engineer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
