        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1450_End12_di" bpmnElement="W1450_End12"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="657" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1450_Annotation13_di" bpmnElement="W1450_Annotation13"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="800" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1450_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1450_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1450_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1450_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1450_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1450_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1450_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1450_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="675" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1450_Flow19_di" bpmnElement="W1450_Flow19"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="675" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="675" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1450_Flow20_di" bpmnElement="W1450_Flow20"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="675" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="675" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1450_Assoc14_di" bpmnElement="W1450_Assoc14"><di:waypoint x="340" y="800" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W5571" name="W5571. Tsunami &amp; Storm-Surge Coastal-Intrusion Response Protocol (PHIVOLCS Advisory / PAGASA Storm-Surge Warning)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: PHIVOLCS tsunami advisory or warning covering any BuildRight coastal site (including the near-field case: a felt earthquake at a coastal site is itself the warning); or a PAGASA significant storm-surge forecast (≥ 2–3 m class) covering a site&#x27;s coastline in the current typhoon track
Frequency: ~60 of ~205 sites sit in coastal municipalities; PAGASA surge warnings accompany the strongest typhoons (several advisory episodes per year chain-wide, most affecting 1–5 sites); tsunami warnings affecting BuildRight sites are rare — distant-basin advisories a few times per decade, a near-field generating quake once in the planning horizon
Volume: 1 event × the affected coastal sites (1–15 stores per surge episode; a near-field tsunami closes an entire coastal band) × the evacuation/hardening move × the documented all-clear gate before re-entry
Owner: Business Continuity Manager / COO (protocol); Store Manager (site execution); Regional Manager (coastal-band supervision)
Participants: Security Guard, HSE Manager (VS-24), Store Manager, DC Manager, Regional Manager, BC Manager, Facilities (W650 make-safe), VS-69 execution chain where the surge rides a typhoon (W2503-class readiness), PNP/BFP/LGU DRRM Office, Structural Engineer (retainer, post-intrusion), Corporate Communications (W855/W134)
Source: workflow W5571 — Tsunami &amp; Storm-Surge Coastal-Intrusion Response Protocol (PHIVOLCS Advisory / PAGASA Storm-Surge Warning)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5571_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5571_Lane1" name="BC Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5571_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5571_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5571_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5571_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5571_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5571_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5571_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5571_Lane3" name="Regional Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5571_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5571_Lane4" name="Facilities">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5571_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5571_Lane5" name="Insurance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5571_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5571_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5571_Start7" name="PHIVOLCS tsunami advisory or warning covering any BuildRight coastal site (including the…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5571_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5571_Task8" name="Monitor &amp; classify">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monitor &amp; classify: the DC command desk and coastal-region managers track PHIVOLCS tsunami messages and PAGASA storm-surge advisories; a felt quake at a coastal site (shaking Intensity IV+ or difficulty standing) triggers Step 2 immediately without waiting for an official message; official advisories classify each site: advisory (prepare), warning 1–3 m (evacuate shoreline-exposed zones), warning &gt; 3 m (full site evacuation)
Responsible (R): BC Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Business Continuity Manager / COO
Duration: Continuous; 5–15 min on event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5571_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5571_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5571_Task9" name="Evacuation / move-up decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Evacuation / move-up decision: horizontal evacuation to the assembly point above surge lines where time allows; vertical move-up (customers and staff to the upper sales level/mezzanine) where it does not; PWD/senior assistance per the W4400 protocols; garden center and lumber-yard staff clear the open-air yard first
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 10–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5571_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5571_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5571_Task10" name="Pre-arrival hardening (time-allowing)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Pre-arrival hardening (time-allowing): kill power at the main where the water path is confirmed; secure the LPG/propane cage (VS-175) and chemical aisles (W1312-class) against flotation and mixing; move critical records and portable tills up; generator fuel topped (W1223) only where the unit sits above surge line
Responsible (R): Store Manager / HSE Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15–40 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5571_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5571_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5571_Task11" name="Accountability &amp; shelter">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Accountability &amp; shelter: assembly/upper-level headcount with the visitor log; comms ring to the Regional Manager and the CMT (W855 activation for multi-site events); no staff re-entry for any reason during the warning window
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: During event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5571_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5571_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5571_Task12" name="All-clear gate">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: All-clear gate: re-entry only after PHIVOLCS cancels the tsunami message (or the surge episode recedes with the LGU DRRM all-clear) AND a walk-down finds no structural undercut, no live utility hazard, and no contaminated standing water beyond the W1312-class response; the gate decision is documented per site
Responsible (R): Regional Manager / Facilities
Accountable (A): Business Continuity Manager / COO
Duration: At all-clear</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5571_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5571_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5571_Task13" name="Salt-intrusion triage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Salt-intrusion triage: any equipment that contacted surge water (generators, switchgear, HVAC, elevators per W5539-class vendor callouts, POS lanes) is de-energized, photographed and scheduled for professional desalination/inspection before re-energization; elevator and escalator units get a licensed-technician release check
Responsible (R): Facilities / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Business Continuity Manager / COO
Duration: 1–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5571_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5571_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5571_Task14" name="Merchandise, claim &amp; closure interface">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Merchandise, claim &amp; closure interface: damaged-stock documentation feeds the W876 claim chain (VS-26); where the surge rode a typhoon, the event merges into the VS-69 recovery chain (W2518/W1552 assessment) with this protocol owning the coastal-water specifics; closure/reopening decisions ride the E-02 custody (W2510/W850)
Responsible (R): Insurance / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: Per recovery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5571_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5571_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5571_Task15" name="After-action &amp; retrofit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: After-action &amp; retrofit: event timeline reviewed against the classification ladder; site surge-readiness items (yard elevation, cage anchoring, generator placement) join the resilience-capex backlog; BCP (W847/W1204) and drill rotation updated
Responsible (R): BC Manager / HSE Manager
Accountable (A): Business Continuity Manager / COO
Duration: 1–3 weeks post-event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5571_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5571_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5571_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5571_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5571_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-319 (ensure controlled execution — BCP Planning &amp; Testing (PA-26.1).) | - operational: all-clear gate decisions documented per site before re-entry; re-energization only after the desalination/inspection record; surge-readiness items tracked to the capex backlog
Owner: Business Continuity Manager / COO (protocol); Store Manager (site execution); Regional Manager (coastal-band supervision)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5571_Assoc18" sourceRef="W5571_Annotation17" targetRef="W5571_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
